      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the usual maximum:\n- **Immediate-release:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Extended-release:** the maximum is 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day, and it is usually given once or twice daily.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of severe GI effects and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total daily, such as 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nPlease tell me which dose you meant. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note."
      }
     ],
